<!--
  VELO Frontend -- IconActivityMood (B57, PROMPT No761)

  The three-state "Мое состояние" glyph set from the owner's `10.svg`, six
  drawings in one component: an OUTLINED circle per mood for the resting state
  and a FILLED one for the selected state.

  Why one component and not six files: these are one artwork set with two
  states, not six independent icons, and the resting/selected pair for a mood
  are genuinely DIFFERENT drawings (measured with getBBox: the resting face is
  64.4% of the circle, the selected face 53.6%) -- so a `selected` prop cannot
  be reduced to a recolour and six near-duplicate wrappers would be worse.

  Path data is lifted VERBATIM from `10.svg` with zero coordinate rewriting --
  each glyph keeps the sheet's own coordinates and is framed by its own
  `viewBox` offset into the 1460x1057 artboard. That is why the numbers below
  look absolute rather than 0-based; do not "normalise" them.

  Colour comes from two CSS variables the caller sets, never a hex: `--vam-face`
  (the circle) and `--vam-ink` (the face). `10.svg` carries one mouth path at
  #4C6689 -- one hex digit off #4C6589 -- and driving everything from one
  variable is what removes that slip.

  Usage: <IconActivityMood mood="good" :selected="true" :size="63" />
-->

